CHAPTER 4: SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
4.1 Architecture Overview

The application follows a web-based client-server architecture.

The browser provides the user interface. JavaScript sends requests to the Flask backend using asynchronous HTTP requests. The backend validates input, prepares financial analysis requests, interacts with the database, and optionally communicates with Gemini AI.

SQLite provides local persistence through SQLAlchemy. Google Sheets can serve as an optional external tracking layer. A rule-based fallback supports core features when AI integration is unavailable.

4.2 Architecture Flow

User
↓
Web Interface (HTML, CSS, JavaScript)
↓
Flask Backend
↓
Input Validation and Financial Processing
↓
SQLite Database through SQLAlchemy
↓
Gemini AI Integration, when configured
↓
Rule-Based Fallback, when required
↓
Budget, Analysis, Suggestions, and Summary
↓
Results displayed to the user

Google Sheets synchronization is an optional integration.

4.3 Main Components

Frontend: Provides forms, financial input fields, and result displays.

Flask Backend: Handles routes, request processing, validation, and financial analysis.

Database Layer: Uses SQLAlchemy and SQLite for local data persistence.

AI Layer: Uses the Google GenAI Python SDK to generate financial insights when configured.

Fallback Layer: Provides rule-based financial planning functionality without requiring an AI API key.

Cloud Integration: Optionally sends tracking data to Google Sheets through Google Apps Script.

CHAPTER 5: MODULE DESCRIPTION
5.1 Income Management

This module accepts the user's monthly income. The income value is used as an input for budgeting and financial analysis.

5.2 Expense Management

Users can organize spending into categories such as rent, food, transportation, dining, entertainment, and utilities. Expense logs can also represent spending recorded over different periods.

5.3 Budget Generation

The budget module uses the supplied income, expenses, and financial goals to produce a structured budget recommendation. Recommendations depend on the application's configured analysis logic.

5.4 Spending Analysis

The analysis module examines the supplied financial data to identify spending patterns and potential areas for improvement.

5.5 Saving Suggestions

This module generates suggestions intended to help users reduce unnecessary spending and work toward their savings goals.

5.6 Financial Reporting

The application can produce monthly financial summaries and reports. Database persistence enables report records to be retained locally.

5.7 Artificial Intelligence Integration

The Gemini integration can generate natural-language financial insights. The model and API key are configurable through environment settings.

5.8 Rule-Based Fallback

When Gemini is not configured or AI access is unavailable, the application can continue supporting core workflows through local rule-based logic. The interface identifies this mode as Rule-Based or Demo mode.

5.9 Google Sheets Integration

An optional Google Apps Script template is provided for connecting the application to a Google Sheet. This integration requires deployment and configuration of the corresponding webhook URL.

