CHAPTER 10: SECURITY AND LIMITATIONS
10.1 Security Considerations
Store API keys in environment variables.
Exclude .env files from version control.
Validate incoming data on the server.
Avoid logging unnecessary sensitive financial information.
Protect public deployments with appropriate security controls.
Use secure HTTPS connections for public access.
Review authentication and access controls before storing real user data.
10.2 Limitations
AI-generated suggestions may not always be accurate.
AI features depend on API availability and configuration.
Rule-based recommendations may be less flexible than AI-generated insights.
The application should not be assumed to provide bank-grade financial management or security.
Optional Google Sheets synchronization requires additional configuration.
Authentication and multi-user access should be verified before use in a shared production environment.
